# Making your first request

This guide fetches a short list of random users from the public API. No authentication required.

## Endpoint

`GET /api/v1/public/randomusers`

Query parameters: `page`, `limit` (strings in the OpenAPI schema — pass numeric strings).

## Examples

<CodeTabs
  examples={[
    {
      label: "cURL",
      language: "bash",
      code: `curl -s "https://praxis-api-kjrf.onrender.com/api/v1/public/randomusers?page=1&limit=3" \\
  -H "Accept: application/json"`,
    },
    {
      label: "JavaScript",
      language: "javascript",
      code: `const res = await fetch(
  "https://praxis-api-kjrf.onrender.com/api/v1/public/randomusers?page=1&limit=3",
  { headers: { Accept: "application/json" } },
);
const body = await res.json();
console.log(body);`,
    },
    {
      label: "TypeScript",
      language: "typescript",
      code: `type PraxisEnvelope<T> = {
  data: T;
  message: string;
  statusCode: number;
  success: boolean;
};

const res = await fetch(
  "https://praxis-api-kjrf.onrender.com/api/v1/public/randomusers?page=1&limit=3",
);
const body = (await res.json()) as PraxisEnvelope<unknown>;
if (!body.success) throw new Error(body.message);
console.log(body.data);`,
    },
    {
      label: "Python",
      language: "python",
      code: `import urllib.request
import json

url = "https://praxis-api-kjrf.onrender.com/api/v1/public/randomusers?page=1&limit=3"
with urllib.request.urlopen(url) as res:
    body = json.load(res)
print(body)`,
    },
  ]}
/>

## What to inspect

- HTTP status (expect `200` on success)
- Envelope fields: `success`, `statusCode`, `message`, `data`
- Pagination behaviour when you change `page` / `limit`

